Capgemini Final Round Interview Experience (5+ Years DevOps)


This round was clearly designed for 5+ years experienced DevOps Engineers 👇

AWS – Advanced Scenario-Based Questions
Design a multi-region, highly available & fault-tolerant architecture.
How will you handle a complete AZ failure in production?
Debugging latency issues in ALB + EC2 + RDS architecture.
Implement secure IAM strategy with least privilege across teams.
How will you design a cost-optimized architecture for high traffic system?

Kubernetes – Production-Level Depth
Write a complete Deployment YAML with:
Probes (Liveness & Readiness)
Resource limits
HPA configuration
Debug a CrashLoopBackOff / OOMKilled pod in production.
Design a multi-tenant Kubernetes cluster.
How will you handle zero-downtime deployments (Rolling, Blue-Green, Canary)?
Troubleshoot networking issues between services (CNI, DNS).

Docker – Real-World Optimization
Write an optimized multi-stage Dockerfile for production.
How to reduce image size & vulnerabilities?
Debug a container working locally but failing in server.
Implement secure container practices (non-root user, minimalistic base image).

Terraform – Enterprise-Level Questions
Write Terraform code for:
Complete infrastructure (VPC, ALB, Auto Scaling, RDS)
How will you manage:
Multiple environments (dev/stage/prod)
Remote backend (S3 + DynamoDB locking)
Handle state drift & conflicts in team environment.
Design modular & reusable Terraform architecture.

Jenkins – Advanced Pipeline Design
Write a full CI/CD pipeline:
Build → Test → Security Scan → Docker → Deploy to Kubernetes
How will you implement:
Parallel stages
Rollback strategy
Troubleshoot pipeline failures in production.
Secure Jenkins (credentials, secrets management).

 Python – DevOps Automation
Write scripts for:
Infrastructure automation (boto3)
